# pytest tmp_path basetemp — pytest roots this at the CWD unless TMPDIR points
# elsewhere, so running the suite from the repo root drops it here (bake tests
# write real PNGs into it). Disposable; also see the "never run pytest through a
# sandbox whose TMPDIR lands in the repo" rule — that once produced real commits.
pytest-of-*/

# Refactor gate snapshot (backend/scripts/refactor_gate.py) — local safety-net
# state, regenerated by `snapshot`/`check`, never a build artifact to publish.
.refactor-gate/

# ── Open-source preparation (see AI-Wall/OPEN-SOURCE-SOMETHING-RARE.md) ─────────
# Infra describing the live server — kept local / in a private repo only.
# NOTE: these are still tracked in git; the public transition removes them from
# history with git-filter-repo. Ignoring here stops any NEW changes from tracking.
backend/ops/
deploy/

# Secrets — wider than the bare `.env` above (keeps *.env.example checked in).
.env.*
*.env
!*.env.example

# Private strategy / business / personal docs — never publish (currently untracked;
# this fence stops an accidental `git add .` from sweeping them into a public repo).
# ⚠️ This file itself ships to the public mirror (`.gitignore` is in PUBLIC_RULES),
# so these patterns are deliberately generic. Naming each document here published
# its title — a CV, a B2B case study — to everyone who cloned the mirror.
#
# ⛔ Do NOT write `docs/` here. It reads like the tidy fix and it silently breaks
# the repository: audits, plans and specs are written into docs/ constantly, and an
# ignored directory makes every NEW one invisible to `git add` with no error. The
# private documents go in docs/private/ instead, which fences them by location
# rather than by title.
#
# Second line of defence, already in place: export-public.sh classifies docs/ as
# NEVER, and the mirror-gate workflow enforces that on every push. Nothing under
# docs/ can reach the public mirror even if it is committed here by accident.
#
# /*.yml is root-anchored (workflows under .github/ are unaffected). If you ever
# need a legitimate root-level .yml, add it with `git add -f` — it will be ignored
# silently otherwise.
.impeccable.md
/*.yml
docs/private/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages.
# Per-plan working directory, never part of the release.
.superpowers/
